    COMMENT: ==================== EXTERNAL (CROSS-APP) DATA ====================
    COMMENT: Read-only access to ANOTHER app's medals, scores and cloud saves.
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: Four components accept an app_id parameter: Medal.getList,
    COMMENT: ScoreBoard.getScores, CloudSave.loadSlot and CloudSave.loadSlots. The other
    COMMENT: app's owner must grant access in their Newgrounds project settings first.
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: These results are passed to the caller and NEVER cached in AppState.
    COMMENT: AppState models exactly one app - the one this client is running as - and
    COMMENT: its session, medal score, host approval and version fields have no foreign
    COMMENT: equivalent. Caching another app's medals there would replace the local list
    COMMENT: wholesale and mark it loaded, so getMedals() would return the wrong app's
    COMMENT: medals. AppState.setValueFromResult rejects foreign results for that
    COMMENT: reason; these methods are the supported way to reach them.
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: Do NOT solve this by adding an app_id parameter to loadMedals(),
    COMMENT: loadSaveSlots() and friends. Those exist to populate the caches, so a
    COMMENT: foreign variant would need a second cache keyed by app id, and every
    COMMENT: reader (getMedals, getMedal, getSaveSlot, hasLoaded) would grow an app id
    COMMENT: argument that is empty for almost every caller. A separate, clearly named,
    COMMENT: uncached surface keeps the common path simple.

    FUNCTION loadExternalMedals(appId: string, callback: function|null = null, thisArg: any = null)

        PURPOSE: Load the medal list belonging to another app.

        PARAMETERS:
            appId: The other app's ID, which must have granted access
            callback: Called with (medals, error)
            thisArg: Scope for the callback

        BEHAVIOR:
            CALL validateExternalAppId(appId)
            CALL executeExternalRead("Medal.getList", { app_id: appId }, "medals", appId, callback, thisArg)

    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION loadExternalScores(appId: string, boardId: number, filters: object|null = null,
                                callback: function|null = null, thisArg: any = null)

        PURPOSE: Load scores from a scoreboard belonging to another app.

        NOTE: the caller must already know the board id. ScoreBoard.getBoards does not
        accept an app_id, so another app's boards cannot be discovered at runtime.

        PARAMETERS:
            appId: The other app's ID, which must have granted access
            boardId: The scoreboard ID, which must belong to that app
            filters: Optional period/limit/skip/tag/user filters, validated exactly as
                     ScoreBoard.getScores validates them
            callback: Called with (scores, error)
            thisArg: Scope for the callback

        BEHAVIOR:
            CALL validateExternalAppId(appId)

            CREATE params AS the normalized filters
            SET params.app_id TO appId
            SET params.id TO boardId

            COMMENT: 'social' is deliberately not supported here. It filters to the
            COMMENT: current user's friends who have played THIS app, which is
            COMMENT: meaningless when the scores belong to a different one.

            CALL executeExternalRead("ScoreBoard.getScores", params, "scores", appId, callback, thisArg)

    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION loadExternalSaveSlots(appId: string, callback: function|null = null, thisArg: any = null)

        PURPOSE: Load the cloud save slot list belonging to another app.

        PARAMETERS:
            appId: The other app's ID, which must have granted access
            callback: Called with (saveSlots, error)
            thisArg: Scope for the callback

        BEHAVIOR:
            CALL validateExternalAppId(appId)
            CALL executeExternalRead("CloudSave.loadSlots", { app_id: appId }, "slots", appId, callback, thisArg)

    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION loadExternalSaveSlot(appId: string, slotId: number, callback: function|null = null, thisArg: any = null)

        PURPOSE: Load a single cloud save slot belonging to another app.

        PARAMETERS:
            appId: The other app's ID, which must have granted access
            slotId: The slot number
            callback: Called with (saveSlot, error)
            thisArg: Scope for the callback

        BEHAVIOR:
            CALL validateExternalAppId(appId)
            CALL executeExternalRead("CloudSave.loadSlot", { app_id: appId, id: slotId }, "slot", appId, callback, thisArg)

    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION validateExternalAppId(appId: string)

        PURPOSE: Reject the two mistakes that would otherwise fail confusingly.

        BEHAVIOR:
            IF core is null THEN
                THROW error "Core not initialized"
            END IF

            IF appId is null OR appId is empty THEN
                THROW error "An external App ID is required"
            END IF

            COMMENT: Passing our own id is a programming error, not a cross-app read. It
            COMMENT: would quietly behave like the ordinary load - except uncached -
            COMMENT: which is a confusing thing to debug later.
            IF appId equals core.appId THEN
                THROW error "That is this app's own ID. Use the ordinary load method instead."
            END IF

    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION executeExternalRead(componentPath: string, params: object, resultProperty: string,
                                 appId: string, callback: function|null, thisArg: any)

        PURPOSE: Shared request/unwrap path for all four cross-app reads.

        PARAMETERS:
            resultProperty: The property on the result model holding the payload

        BEHAVIOR:
            CALL core.callComponent(componentPath, params, FUNCTION(response)

                IF callback is null THEN
                    RETURN
                END IF

                CREATE error AS null
                CREATE payload AS null

                COMMENT: A cross-app read can be refused at either level: the request may
                COMMENT: fail outright, or succeed while the component reports that access
                COMMENT: was not granted. Check both so the caller gets one clear answer.
                IF response is null OR response.success is not true THEN
                    SET error TO response.error IF PRESENT OTHERWISE Errors.getError()
                ELSE
                    CREATE result AS response.getResult()

                    IF result is null THEN
                        SET error TO Errors.getError(Errors.INVALID_RESPONSE)
                    ELSE IF result.success is not true THEN
                        SET error TO result.error IF PRESENT OTHERWISE Errors.getError()
                    ELSE
                        SET payload TO result[resultProperty]
                        CALL stampForeign(payload, appId)
                    END IF
                END IF

                CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING payload, error

            END FUNCTION)

    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION stampForeign(value: any, appId: string)

        PURPOSE: Mark a returned model, and everything nested inside it, as belonging to
        another app, by setting BaseObject.foreignAppId.

        WHY: Recursive because the interesting objects are often nested - a score list
        carries a User per Score, and a getScores result carries the ScoreBoard. A caller
        holding any of those should be able to tell where it came from.

        BEHAVIOR:
            IF value is null THEN
                RETURN
            END IF

            IF value is an array THEN
                FOR EACH item IN value
                    CALL stampForeign(item, appId)
                END FOR
                RETURN
            END IF

            IF value is not a BaseObject THEN
                RETURN
            END IF

            SET value.foreignAppId TO appId

            FOR EACH propertyName IN value.propertyNames
                CALL stampForeign(value[propertyName], appId)
            END FOR

    END FUNCTION

    COMMENT: ==================== SERVER UTILITIES & EVENTS ====================
    COMMENT: Methods for server time synchronization, connectivity testing, and custom event tracking.
    COMMENT: These are utility functions for advanced features.
    
    COMMENT: The next three methods all call the SAME component, Gateway.getDatetime,
    COMMENT: and differ only in how they present its result. Implement them as three
    COMMENT: thin wrappers over one shared private routine (see
    COMMENT: executeGatewayDateTime below) rather than three copies of the same call.

    FUNCTION loadGatewayDateTime(callback: function, thisArg: any = null)

        PURPOSE: Get current server time as an ISO 8601 string.
        PARAMETERS:
            callback: (required) Function called with (dateTime, error)
            thisArg: (optional, default: null) Context to use when calling the callback
        CALLBACK PARAMETERS:
            dateTime: string|null - ISO 8601 server time, null on failure
            error: NewgroundsIO.models.objects.Error|null - null on success

        BEHAVIOR:
            CALL executeGatewayDateTime(callback, thisArg, "datetime")
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION loadGatewayTimestamp(callback: function, thisArg: any = null)

        PURPOSE: Get current server time as a UNIX timestamp (seconds).
        PARAMETERS:
            callback: (required) Function called with (timestamp, error)
            thisArg: (optional, default: null) Context to use when calling the callback
        CALLBACK PARAMETERS:
            timestamp: number|null - seconds since the epoch, null on failure
            error: NewgroundsIO.models.objects.Error|null - null on success

        BEHAVIOR:
            CALL executeGatewayDateTime(callback, thisArg, "timestamp")
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION loadGatewayDate(callback: function, thisArg: any = null)

        PURPOSE: Get current server time as your platform's native date type.
        WHY: Most callers want a date object they can format or compare, not a string
        to parse. Skip this method only if your language has no native date type.
        PARAMETERS:
            callback: (required) Function called with (date, error)
            thisArg: (optional, default: null) Context to use when calling the callback
        CALLBACK PARAMETERS:
            date: Date|null - native date built from the server timestamp, null on failure
            error: NewgroundsIO.models.objects.Error|null - null on success

        BEHAVIOR:
            CALL executeGatewayDateTime(callback, thisArg, "date")
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION sendPing(callback: function|null = null, thisArg: any = null)
        
        PURPOSE: Send a simple ping to test server connectivity.
        PARAMETERS:
            callback: (optional, default: null) Function called with (pong, error)
            thisArg: (optional, default: null) Context to use when calling the callback
        CALLBACK PARAMETERS:
            pong: (required) A simple string 'pong' indicating successful connection
            error: (optional, default: null) Error object if something went wrong, or null on success
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            IF core is null THEN
                THROW error "Core not initialized"
            END IF
            
            CREATE component AS CALL ObjectFactory.CreateComponent("Gateway", "ping", null, core)
            IF component is null THEN
                THROW error "Could not create Gateway.ping component"
            END IF
            
            CALL core.executeComponent(component, 
                FUNCTION onComplete(result)
                    IF callback is null THEN RETURN END IF
                    
                    IF result is null THEN
                        CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING null, null
                        RETURN
                    END IF
                    
                    CREATE error AS null
                    IF result.error is not null THEN
                        SET error TO result.error
                    END IF
                    
                    CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING 'pong', error
                END FUNCTION
            )
    END FUNCTION
    
    FUNCTION logEvent(eventName: string, callback: function|null = null, thisArg: any = null)
        
        PURPOSE: Log a custom event to server for tracking.
        PARAMETERS:
            eventName: (required) Name of the event to log
            callback: (optional, default: null) Function called with (error)
            thisArg: (optional, default: null) Context to use when calling the callback
        CALLBACK PARAMETERS:
            error: (optional, default: null) Error object if something went wrong, or null on success
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            IF core is null THEN
                THROW error "Core not initialized"
            END IF
            
            CREATE component AS CALL ObjectFactory.CreateComponent("Event", "logEvent", null, core)
            IF component is null THEN
                THROW error "Could not create Event.logEvent component"
            END IF
            SET component.host TO (core.appState.host IF NOT NULL, OTHERWISE "N/A")
            SET component.event_name TO eventName
            
            CALL core.executeComponent(component, 
                FUNCTION onComplete(result)
                    IF callback is not null THEN
                        CREATE error AS null
                        IF result is not null AND result.error is not null THEN
                            SET error TO result.error
                        END IF
                        CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING error
                    END IF
                END FUNCTION
            )
    END FUNCTION
    
    COMMENT: ==================== URL NAVIGATION ====================
    COMMENT: Methods for opening and loading various URLs.
    COMMENT: NOTE: Some platforms have security restrictions on programmatic URL opening.
    
    FUNCTION openOfficialUrl(target: string = "_blank", logEvent: boolean = true)
        
        PURPOSE: Open URL where latest official version can be found in a new window/tab.
        NOTE: Some platforms have security restrictions on programmatic URL opening.
        PARAMETERS:
            target: (optional, default: platform default) Window/tab target for opening URL
            logEvent: (optional, default: true) Log this action
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            IF core is null THEN
                THROW error "Core not initialized"
            END IF
            
            IF target is null THEN
                SET target TO "_blank"
            END IF
            IF logEvent is null THEN
                SET logEvent TO true
            END IF
            
            CREATE component AS CALL ObjectFactory.CreateComponent("Loader", "loadOfficialUrl", null, core)
            IF component is null THEN
                THROW error "Could not create Loader.loadOfficialUrl component"
            END IF
            
            SET component.host TO (core.appState.host IF NOT NULL, OTHERWISE "N/A")
            SET component.browserTarget TO target
            SET component.log_stat TO logEvent
            SET component.redirect TO true
            
            CALL core.executeComponent(component, null)
    END FUNCTION
    
    FUNCTION loadOfficialUrl(logEvent: boolean = true, callback: function|null = null, thisArg: any = null)
        
        PURPOSE: Load URL where latest official version can be found (asynchronously).
        PARAMETERS:
            logEvent: (optional, default: true) Log this action
            callback: (optional, default: null) Function called with (url, error)
            thisArg: (optional, default: null) Context to use when calling the callback
        CALLBACK PARAMETERS:
            url: (required) String - The URL to open
            error: (optional, default: null) Error - Error object if something went wrong
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            IF core is null THEN
                THROW error "Core not initialized"
            END IF
            
            IF logEvent is null THEN
                SET logEvent TO true
            END IF
            
            CREATE component AS CALL ObjectFactory.CreateComponent("Loader", "loadOfficialUrl", null, core)
            IF component is null THEN
                THROW error "Could not create Loader.loadOfficialUrl component"
            END IF
            
            SET component.host TO (core.appState.host IF NOT NULL, OTHERWISE "N/A")
            SET component.log_stat TO logEvent
            SET component.redirect TO false
            
            CALL core.executeComponent(component, 
                FUNCTION onComplete(result)
                    IF callback is null THEN RETURN END IF
                    
                    IF result is null THEN
                        CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING null, null
                        RETURN
                    END IF
                    
                    CREATE error AS null
                    IF result.error is not null THEN
                        SET error TO result.error
                    END IF
                    
                    CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING result.url, error
                END FUNCTION
            )
    END FUNCTION
    
    FUNCTION openAuthorUrl(target: string = "_blank", logEvent: boolean = true)
        
        PURPOSE: Open author's home page URL in a new browser window.
        NOTE: URL opening must be triggered by user interaction in many platforms (security requirement).
        PARAMETERS:
